@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant — same flow modeled as UML activity vs SysML activity.
'   usecase:      Show delta: rate, «continuous», «controlOperator» are SysML-only additions.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       systems-engineering
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Activity - SysML vs UML Activity (Variant)

' Two swimlane treatments of the same "fill a tank" control loop.
' Left lane = plain UML (control/object flow only).
' Right lane = SysML (adds «continuous», rate, «controlOperator»).

|UML Activity|
' Pure discrete control/object flow. No stereotypes, no rates, no
' on/off enablement semantics.
start
:Read Setpoint;
:Read Level;
:Compute Error;
if (Error > 0?) then (yes)
  :Open Valve;
else (no)
  :Close Valve;
endif
:Log State;
stop

|SysML Activity|
' Same skeleton, plus SysML extensions.
start
:Read Setpoint;
:Receive Level
  <<continuous>>
  {rate = 10 Hz};
:Compute Error;
:<<controlOperator>>
EnableValve;
if (Error > 0?) then (yes)
  :Open Valve;
  :Flow Fluid
    <<continuous>>
    {rate = 5 L/s};
else (no)
  :Close Valve;
endif
:<<controlOperator>>
DisableValve;
:Log State;
stop

note right of |SysML Activity|
  <b>Delta (SysML adds):</b>
  1. «continuous» / «discrete» stereotypes
  2. {rate=N} annotations on flows
  3. «controlOperator» — enable/disable
     rather than data flow
  4. «callBehavior» nested activities
  (used in complex example)
end note

@enduml
